# NyxHop board on a Mark4 7-inch quad: the PX4 parameters of this aircraft, on top of the board's
# own (nyxhop-bb.config). README.md beside this file says why each one is what it is.
#
#   python fc/install.py params <board address> fc/aircraft/mark4-7inch/mark4.params
#
# NAME VALUE on a line; # starts a comment.

# Motors, numbered as the ESC port's M1..M4 are wired: 1 front left, 2 front right, 3 rear left,
# 4 rear right. Position from the centre in metres (PX forward, PY to the right); KM is negative
# for a motor that turns clockwise seen from above.
CA_ROTOR0_PX      0.0965
CA_ROTOR0_PY     -0.1115
CA_ROTOR0_KM     -0.05
CA_ROTOR1_PX      0.0965
CA_ROTOR1_PY      0.1115
CA_ROTOR1_KM      0.05
CA_ROTOR2_PX     -0.0965
CA_ROTOR2_PY     -0.1115
CA_ROTOR2_KM      0.05
CA_ROTOR3_PX     -0.0965
CA_ROTOR3_PY      0.1115
CA_ROTOR3_KM     -0.05

# Thrust: it hovers at a quarter of full throttle on 4S; the take-off climbs at 2 m/s.
MPC_THR_HOVER     0.25
MPC_TKO_SPEED     2

# Battery: warn at 25 %, critical at 15 %, emergency at 8 %.
BAT_LOW_THR       0.25
BAT_CRIT_THR      0.15
BAT_EMERGEN_THR   0.08

# Compass of the GPS module (arrow to the nose): its chip sits rolled 180 and yawed 90 degrees.
CAL_MAG0_ROT      10

# Height: the board has no barometer, the MTF-01's range finder is the height reference.
SYS_HAS_BARO      0
EKF2_BARO_CTRL    0
EKF2_HGT_REF      2
EKF2_RNG_CTRL     2
EKF2_MIN_RNG      0.09
EKF2_RNG_FOG      0

# Optical flow: on the ground only over a surface it sees well.
EKF2_OF_QMIN_GND  60

# Estimator: the accelerometer's offset moves with the board's temperature, and the aircraft
# stands with its motors running for a few seconds before it lifts off.
EKF2_ACC_B_NOISE  0.01
EKF2_ABL_LIM      0.8
EKF2_NOAID_TOUT   10000000
